 {"status": "in_progress", "id": "AUG-138", "title": "[R8] XML spec blocks cannot reference DuckBrain decision records, so the spec cannot overlay the ledger it annotates", "detail": {"fingerprint": "8f5192fcefce7c3783a4a88190395b6f0354cacf7acb1f99cf0c7554f64a40ee"}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05 at HEAD c7ff7f7: `grep -cE 'decision-ref|record-ref|decision_ref|record_ref' auger.py specs/schema/auger-spec-1.0.xsd` -> 0 in both files. SPEC_EDGE_ATTRS holds only depends-on/verifies/refs/implements/supersedes, all of which resolve INSIDE the corpus, and no spec-path code queries the DuckBrain namespace at all. PRD R8 says DuckBrain stays authoritative and XML references stable record IDs; today the two halves of the product (decision ledger and authored spec) have no typed seam, so a spec block cannot say 'this requirement rests on decision D-014, and here is why the alternatives lost'. The audit scored R8 ABSENT and no board row named it.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a typed reference attribute (e.g. decision-ref / record-ref) exists in SPEC_EDGE_ATTRS and in specs/schema/auger-spec-1.0.xsd, and the XSD-vs-constants parity test covers its enum/shape.\nPASS: the resolver checks the named record in a DuckBrain namespace and REFUSES a corpus whose reference names a nonexistent record - rc 2, typed code, naming document + block id + the missing record id - proven by a fixture that points at a record that does not exist.\nPASS: a superseded record is reported as a typed diagnostic (not silently accepted), proven by a fixture against a namespace that holds a superseded record.\nPASS: the read path never writes: a test asserts zero mutating requests to DuckBrain during validate / assemble / check (the corpus tree hash is also unchanged).\nPASS: an offline/missing-substrate run fails with a named substrate error, not a silent pass.", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:06:15.188275+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-06T22:12:32.858429+00:00", "foreman_note": "DISPATCHED SG9 (2026-11-06) from base b93630b; brief ~/.hermes/goals/auger-xml-hardening-SG9-brief.txt, evidence target ~/.hermes/goals/evidence/auger-SG9/. Driver-measured baseline: grep -c 'decision-ref|record-ref' auger.py specs/schema/auger-spec-1.0.xsd -> 0/0; SPEC_EDGE_ATTRS at auger.py:7748 holds only depends-on/verifies/refs/implements/supersedes. Traps written into the brief: the XSD is now LOADED, so the new attribute must be declared in specs/schema/auger-spec-1.0.xsd or every document refuses schema-invalid; a corpus with no decision-ref must stay substrate-free and hermetic.\n\nSG9 LANDED 2026-11-06, awaiting a commit-bound GitReins verdict (debt AUG-154). Commit 5fb72e3 on main (merge 5b0518c). Driver probes on the merged tree: (1) a decision-ref corpus with no --decision-namespace refuses rc 2 typed missing-decision-namespace naming document+block+record; (2) --decision-namespace <namespace without the record> refuses rc 2 typed decision-ledger-unavailable (fail closed, never a silent pass); (3) validate and check return the SAME typed refusal; (4) the shipped corpus still validates rc 0. New file tests/test_spec_decision_ref.py is named in tests/gate.sh's pytest arm; its 2 live tests resolved a real record and reported a superseded one (~/.hermes/goals/evidence/auger-SG9/probe-AUG-138-live.txt). Gate: worktree PASS 625/901.55s; merged main PASS 625/917.00s rc 0.", "capability_tags": [], "worktree": "/home/kara/proj-wt-auger-xml-hardening", "branch": "wt/auger-xml-hardening"}
 {"status": "in_progress", "id": "AUG-139", "title": "[AC-5] No view-regeneration path and no source-mutation test: 'Markdown/HTML are generated views of XML' is unproven", "detail": {"fingerprint": "e6ae1a450d51578865e4edc04fd0c5cf2079e94596f9349d8d05089defb824ad"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05 at HEAD c7ff7f7: `auger spec --help` exposes validate/list/assemble/check/bundle and no verb writes a rendered view; `tests/fixtures/xml/expected/` holds ONE golden (assembly-active-auger-export.md) and `grep -c regenerat` over the board rows -> 0. Q2 of the 2026-11-05 audit is exactly this: render_spec_assembly is deterministic, but no test mutates a source block and asserts the rendered view changed, so a regression that emitted a cached or stale body would pass all XML tests. PRD AC-5 names a multi-view regeneration fixture plus a source-only mutation test; neither exists, and no row names it.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: a documented verb (e.g. `auger spec render <dir> --out <dir>`) regenerates every view it ships (at least Markdown, plus the second view the PRD names) from the XML source, and two consecutive runs are byte-identical (sha256 equal) - asserted in a test.\nPASS: a source-mutation test mutates ONE block body in the input corpus and asserts the regenerated views change for that block and stay byte-identical for untouched blocks.\nPASS: the mutation test is proven load-bearing - with the renderer pinned to a stale/cached body the test FAILS; the before/after transcript is kept as evidence.\nPASS: the render path is read-only on the corpus (tree hash before/after equal) and refuses to write into the corpus root.\nPASS: the new test file is named by tests/gate.sh's pytest arm (a suite not in that list is never run).", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:06:15.219269+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-07T01:37:37.712523+00:00", "foreman_note": "Driver verification at 8e1139bf (not the worker's report): render rc0 twice, md/html sha256 equal across runs; committed views byte-identical to a fresh render; corpus tree-hash unchanged (read-only); --out inside the corpus root refused rc2 render-into-corpus; SOURCE MUTATION - injected a sentinel into SPEC-GRAPH-CORPUS's body, re-rendered, sentinel present in BOTH views with the untouched block's 12 render lines unchanged; tests/test_spec_render.py (12 tests) named in tests/gate.sh's pytest arm with a test_gate_arm_runs_this_file assertion. Transcripts: ~/.hermes/goals/sg10-driver-mutation.txt, sg10-gate-wt.log (650 passed), sg10-gate-main-run2.log (650 passed).", "capability_tags": [], "worker_status": "done", "commit_hash": "c6ed304", "guard_result": "SKIP", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "Landed c6ed304 (SG10): 'auger spec render <root> --out <dir>' regenerates BOTH shipped views (SPEC-CORPUS-VIEW.md + new .html) from the one load_spec_corpus path; gen_spec_view.py is a thin front end. VERDICT OUTSTANDING: no commit-bound GitReins verdict exists, so no evidence-run-id was supplied (verdict debt AUG-154)."}
 {"status": "in_progress", "id": "AUG-140", "title": "[AC-14] Assembly JSON reports counts only: no input/output bytes, no elapsed time, no proof unselected bodies were skipped", "detail": {"fingerprint": "dd8a2a9cf9895b012b98c5766f6f96b11c2e378c9c4f907404fc8b208196b449"}, "priority": "P2", "source": null, "reasoning": "Measured 2026-11-05 at HEAD c7ff7f7: `auger spec assemble tests/fixtures/xml/specs --applies-to auger.export --format json` emits exactly ['blocks','counts','schema_version','selection'] with counts={'matched','dependencies','total'}. No input bytes, no output bytes, no elapsed time, and no assertion that unselected block bodies were not parsed (the loader rglobs and parses every *.xml). PRD AC-14 asks for a JSON report with bytes and elapsed time, and success proof 7 says do not claim savings without measuring bytes - so today the PRD's own value claim is unmeasurable. AUG-137 records this inside its reasoning but no row owns the measurement.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: the assembly JSON carries input_bytes, output_bytes, documents_read, blocks_parsed and elapsed_ms alongside the existing keys, with the report schema version bumped and documented.\nPASS: the numbers are real, asserted in a test: output_bytes == len(serialized output) and input_bytes == the sum of the corpus file sizes actually read.\nPASS: a test proves unselected bodies are not parsed - e.g. blocks_parsed <= matched+closure for a corpus holding many more blocks than the selector matches, and the test goes red if a full-corpus parse is reintroduced.\nPASS: elapsed_ms is measured around the real assembly, not a constant (test asserts it varies / is >= 0 and > 0 on a corpus above a size floor).\nPASS: `auger spec assemble --format json` on the shipped fixture still exits 0 and its blocks are unchanged (no behaviour change disguised as instrumentation).", "complexity": 3, "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:06:15.244845+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-07T01:37:37.804844+00:00", "foreman_note": "Driver-measured at 8e1139bf on tests/fixtures/xml/specs: output_bytes 3220 == emitted file size 3220; input_bytes 4098 == actual corpus bytes (3 files, documents_read 3); blocks_parsed 6 <= matched 6 + closure 0 with blocks_indexed 10 on the whole corpus (laziness real); elapsed_ms present and >=0; blocks identical to the default run; default JSON keys remain the documented five (blocks, corpus, counts, schema_version, selection), rc 0. tests/test_spec_assembly_report.py (12 tests) named in the gate pytest arm. Logs: sg10-gate-wt.log, sg10-gate-main-run2.log.", "capability_tags": [], "worker_status": "done", "commit_hash": "c6ed304", "guard_result": "SKIP", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "Landed c6ed304 (SG10): assemble --format json --measure adds report_schema_version 1.1, input_bytes, output_bytes, documents_read, blocks_indexed, blocks_parsed, elapsed_ms, via a new indexed loader that materializes only selected bodies. Report is OPT-IN, disclosed: a default elapsed_ms would break AC-4's byte identity. VERDICT OUTSTANDING: no GitReins verdict (debt AUG-154)."}
